---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const stats = [
  { num: "15+", label: "Years in enterprise tech" },
  { num: "6", label: "Acquisitions in under 2 years" },
  { num: "27", label: "Countries delivered across" },
  { num: "500+", label: "Consultants in the practice built" },
];
---

<Base
  title="About — Kaizen Blue"
  description="Kaizen Blue is a technology strategy and consulting firm founded by Daniel Da Vinci, working at the intersection of enterprise technology, cloud, and AI."
>
  <section class="pagehead">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h1 class="h1">Small by design. Built to get things done.</h1>
      <p class="lead pagehead__intro">
        Kaizen Blue is a technology strategy and consulting firm founded by
        Daniel Da Vinci. We work at the intersection of enterprise technology,
        cloud, and AI.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="stats">
        {
          stats.map((s) => (
            <div class="stat">
              <div class="stat__num">{s.num}</div>
              <div class="stat__label">{s.label}</div>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>The real version</h2>
        <p>
          I started Kaizen Blue because I was tired of watching big
          consultancies charge millions for slide decks that never get executed.
          I'd spent years inside the machine: running SAP cloud transformations,
          leading a global practice at SoftwareONE, buying and integrating six
          companies across five continents. I knew what good looked like. I also
          knew that most of the industry was selling process, not progress.
        </p>
        <p>
          So I built something different. Kaizen Blue is small by design. We
          don't have 500 consultants and a bench to fill. We have deep
          expertise, a bias toward action, and a track record of getting things
          done.
        </p>
        <p>
          The name comes from <strong>kaizen</strong>, the Japanese philosophy
          of continuous improvement. That's how we operate. Not big bang
          transformations that take three years and cost a fortune. Steady,
          relentless progress. Every week better than the last.
        </p>

        <h2>About Daniel</h2>
        <p>
          15+ years in enterprise technology. I've run SAP cloud
          transformations for Fortune 500 clients across APAC, EMEA, and the
          Americas. At SoftwareONE I led the global SAP Services practice and
          drove six acquisitions in under two years: BNW (Australia), Optimum
          Consulting (US), ITPC (Switzerland), ITST (Brazil), SE16N (Poland),
          and Centiq (UK). That built a 500+ consultant practice across 27
          countries. I also secured the strategic partnership with Microsoft for
          SAP on Azure.
        </p>
        <p>
          Now I'm deep in AI. I completed Harvard Business School's AI for
          Business Leaders program and went straight into building. I run LLMs,
          agentic workflows, and intelligent automation across Kaizen Blue, and
          I'm driving AI ops in enterprise environments at Syensqo. I build with
          AI every day. Not from a slide deck. From a terminal.
        </p>
        <p>
          I push performance in everything I touch. Strategy, execution,
          technology, people. I don't sit in advisory mode and hand over a PDF.
          I get in, I figure it out, I make it work.
        </p>

        <h3>Previously</h3>
        <p>
          SoftwareONE (Global SAP Practice Leader), SAP (Technology Consultant),
          plus work with Microsoft and various enterprise clients globally.
        </p>
        <p>Based in Singapore and Japan.</p>
        <p>
          LinkedIn:
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/davincidaniel" rel="noopener" target="_blank">
            linkedin.com/in/davincidaniel
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="cta-band">
        <h2 class="h2">Want to put that experience to work?</h2>
        <p>No pitch decks, no sales process. Just a conversation.</p>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn--primary btn--lg">
          Get in touch <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
